## IV. Cursor Capability and Tool Routing

> Rewritten for Cursor Harness. Claude’s `@capability-index.md` is **not** imported here (Cursor Rules do not hard-inline `@file` the Claude way). Maintain this section when MCP / Skills / subagents change.

### §1 Asset Map (where things live)

| Asset | Cursor path | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Global rules entry | `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\rules\AGENTS.mdc` | `alwaysApply: true` — this file |
| Parallel doc copy | `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\AGENTS.md` | Same body without Rule frontmatter; keep in sync |
| Companion rules | `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\rules\*.mdc` | e.g. `answer-format`, Windows shell/path, commit-history |
| MCP config | `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\mcp.json` | Standard `mcpServers` schema |
| Cursor-native skills | `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\skills-cursor\` | create-rule / create-skill / canvas / … |
| Shared skills pool | `%USERPROFILE%\.agents\skills\` · `%USERPROFILE%\.claude\skills\` | Discoverable; prefer Cursor-relevant skills; do not assume Claude hooks apply |
| Project rules | `<repo>\.cursor\rules\` | Project overrides when workspace is a repo |

### §2 Skills and Documentation
- When a relevant Skill exists under `skills-cursor` or shared skills, **read and follow it** before improvising.
- For Cursor product questions (settings, Agent, hooks, Bugbot), use the `cursor-guide` skill/subagent.
- For library/framework docs: prefer MCP / web tools available in-session; do not invent APIs.
- Prefer progressive disclosure: load a skill when the task matches its description — do not dump every skill into every turn.

### §3 Tool Selection (Cursor-native names)
- **Workspace root**: If work belongs to a project folder, call `cursor-app-control.move_agent_to_root` **before** substantive edits (home-directory rule).
- **Files**: `Glob` / `Grep` / `Read` / `Write` / `StrReplace`; shell via `Shell` (obey Windows path/shell discipline rules).
- **Dynamic tools / MCP**: Discover schema with `GetDynamicTools`, then invoke via `CallDynamicTool`. Never guess argument shapes.
- **Subagents**: Use `Task` with the listed `subagent_type` values (explore, cursor-guide, bugbot, security-review, …). Link agent ids in user-facing text when required by the platform.
- **Browser / mermaid preview**: Use available MCP namespaces (e.g. `plugin-claude-mermaid-mermaid`) when diagram preview is needed; CLI replies must not dump unrenderable Mermaid.
- **Media**: MiniMax MCP for image/video/audio/music when configured; `minimax-coding.understand_image` for vision fallback; `icons` for Lucide (site UI assets — follow `lucide-icons` skill).
- Prefer built-in tools over MCP when they overlap (same wisdom as Kimi’s tool blacklist): avoid duplicate “filesystem” MCP if Shell/Read already cover the job.

### §4 MCP Routing (this machine’s Cursor profile)
Configured in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` (enablement may vary by session):

| Scenario | Preferred | Fallback |
|---|---|---|
| Image / video / TTS / music generation | `MiniMax` | Ask user; do not fake URLs |
| Image understanding (text-only model) | `minimax-coding.understand_image` | User-supplied description |
| Web search (if exposed) | `minimax-coding.web_search` / Cursor `WebSearch` | State gap if unavailable |
| Lucide icons | `icons` + skill `lucide-icons` | — |
| App control (root / project / dialog) | `cursor-app-control` | — |
| Mermaid live preview | `plugin-claude-mermaid-mermaid` | ASCII / numbered steps |

Do not enable or invent MCP servers that are not listed in the active session namespaces. Credentials live in MCP/env config — never print secrets.

### §5 Configuration Hygiene and Harness Boundary
- Before editing global config, identify the **active entry** (`AGENTS.mdc` vs User Rules vs project rules), duplicates, and last write time.
- Coexist with Claude Code / OpenCode / Kimi: do **not** execute Claude hooks, do not assume `~/.claude/settings.json` applies inside Cursor, do not symlink entire Claude plugin trees into `.cursor` without a Cursor-native install path.
- Treat tokens, cookies, API keys, and auth caches as sensitive; never echo original values.
- Before deleting residual config, produce a read-only candidate list and get explicit user confirmation.
- Before claiming completion: fresh diff or equivalent check; report files changed and remaining gaps (e.g. Cursor User Rules copy may still lag until manually refreshed).
